 "title": "Turkeys can't fly? Wild ones hit 55 mph 🦃",
 "description": "Happy Thanksgiving! Wild turkeys can run up to 25 mph and fly in short bursts at up to 55 mph, often about 100 yards at a time, and every night they fly up into trees to roost. The turkey on your plate is a different story: farm turkeys are bred for bigger breasts and legs, weigh about 20-35 lb alive, and are too heavy to fly.\n\nSources: PBS Nature (wild turkey fact sheet); Live Science; Popular Science; National Wild Turkey Federation.",
